<title>UK: UK output prices fall 0.1 pct in March.</title>
<headline>UK output prices fall 0.1 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following provisional data on UK input and output prices in March (previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    OUTPUT PRICES (unadj) MARCH    FEB   (PREL FEB)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  -0.1    -0.1    (UNCH)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	    1.0	1.2     (1.3)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     124.8    124.9 (125.0)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO PETROLEUM (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  0.2	0.1     (0.1)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	    0.5	0.5     (0.5)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     120.6    120.3 (120.3)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD,DRINK,TOBACCO,PETROLEUM (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  0.1	0.1     (0.1)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	    0.5	0.6     (O.6)</p>
<p>    Qtr/qtr change	  0.1	0.2     (0.2)</p>
<p>    Qtr/Qtr annual rate   0.2	0.7     (0.7)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     120.3    120.2 (120.2)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	 -0.9     -1.4    (-0.9)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	   -7.6     -6.8    (-6.6)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     106.9    107.9 (108.2)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	 -0.5     -0.7    (-0.5)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	   -7.7     -6.9    (-6.6)</p>
<p>    Index		     106.6   107.1   (107.4)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F,D,T,P (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	 -0.7     -1.0    (-0.5)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	   -6.7     -7.6    (-7.4)</p>
<p>    Index		     104.0   104.7  (104.9)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F,D,T,P (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  0.4     -0.3    (UNCH)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr  change	  -6.6     -7.4    (-7.4)</p>
<p>    Index		     104.3    103.9  (103.9)</p>
<p>    INPUT COMPONENTS PCT CHANGE    MARCH M/M     MARCH Y/Y</p>
<p>    fuel				    -4.0	 -2.7</p>
<p>    crude oil etc			 -7.8	 -6.5</p>
<p>    food(home produced)		  0.8	 -11.2</p>
<p>    food (imported)			1.7	 -2.5</p>
<p>    metals				   1.5	 -9.7</p>
<p>    chemicals			     -0.4	 -9.0</p>
<p>    other imported materials	   unch	-7.8</p>
<p>Consensus of economists' forecasts was for input prices to rise a seasonally adjusted 0.2 percent and fall 6.5 percent year-on-year. Output prices forecast +0.1 on the month, +1.2 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>The ONS said a fall in the price of crude oil and a seasonal fall in the cost of electricity to industrial customers were mainly responsible for lower input prices in March.</p>
</text>
